---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { config } from '../config';

const { responsibleParty, lastUpdated, messageRetentionDays } = config.privacy;
const email = config.contactEmail;
const isDraft = responsibleParty === '' || !email;
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What personal information OpenForge collects, why, who it is shared with, and your rights under POPIA.">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>
    How OpenForge handles personal information, in line with South Africa's Protection of Personal
    Information Act (POPIA). Last updated: {lastUpdated}.
  </p>

  {isDraft && (
    <p class="notice">Draft policy. Add the responsible party and a contact email in src/config.ts before launch.</p>
  )}

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {responsibleParty} is the responsible party for personal information collected through this
      site. Send privacy questions and requests to
      {' '}{email ? <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> : '(email not added yet)'}.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

    <h3>Visiting the site</h3>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider, Vercel, processes technical data such as your IP address, browser type
      and the pages you request, so that the site can be delivered and kept secure. We do not run
      analytics or advertising trackers.
    </p>

    <h3>The contact form</h3>
    <p>
      If you send a message through the contact form, we collect your name, your email address,
      optionally your organisation, your message, and a record that you ticked the consent box, with
      the time. We use these to read and reply to your message, and for nothing else. Each message is
      stored as a private issue in a GitHub repository that only the site owner can open, and GitHub
      emails the owner a notice of it.
    </p>

    <h3>Email and phone</h3>
    <p>If you email or phone us instead, we use the details you give to reply.</p>

    <h3>Security check</h3>
    <p>
      The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from bots. It loads from Cloudflare
      only when you start filling in the form. Cloudflare processes information about your browser
      and device for that purpose, under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Our legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      We process the information in your message with your consent. We also process technical data
      where it is needed to run and secure the site, which is a legitimate interest that does not
      unreasonably affect your privacy.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal information. These providers process it for us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Vercel: hosting.</li>
      <li>GitHub: the private repository that holds incoming messages.</li>
      <li>Google (Gmail): receiving notices of new messages and sending replies.</li>
      <li>Cloudflare: the Turnstile security check.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Transfers outside South Africa</h2>
    <p>
      These providers may store and process information in other countries, including the United
      States. We cannot control where they keep it, so the form asks for your consent and names this
      transfer before you send anything.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Messages: kept until the conversation has ended, then deleted from the inbox within {messageRetentionDays} days. Email copies of the notice and our replies are deleted on the
        same schedule.
      </li>
      <li>Server logs: kept by our hosting provider under its own retention schedule.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Access to the inbox is limited to the site owner, and the site connects to it with an access
      token limited to that one repository. No system is completely secure. If a breach affects your
      personal information, we will notify the Information Regulator and, where required, you.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask what personal information we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Ask us to correct or delete it.</li>
      <li>
        Object to processing, or withdraw your consent at any time, by emailing us. Withdrawing does
        not affect processing that already happened lawfully.
      </li>
      <li>
        Complain to the Information Regulator at{' '}<a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener noreferrer">inforegulator.org.za</a>.
        We would appreciate the chance to fix the problem first.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not intended for children under 18, and they should not use the contact form.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
